{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1198723-awakening-kindred-devoured-werewolves-and-other-hybrids","id":1198723,"title":"Awakening Kindred, Devoured Werewolves, and other Hybrids","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-23T09:59:36-07:00","id":1198723,"title":"Awakening Kindred, Devoured Werewolves, and other Hybrids","content":"I gotta admit, I like the concept of mixing splats up to make something strange and new. The Admontoria were something I throughly enjoyed, and I think concepts like the Crone/Wyrm Mage/Beast Hybrids are fun and make for an excellent addition to a game, especially if you have a troupe that's well-versed in the ChroD. This is why I thought it might be nice to dedicate a thread to gathering ideas, potentially working a select few out some more =)<br /> If nothing else, working this stuff out gives me a deeper appreciation of the different games' themes and moods.<br /> Of course, one should look to Hybrids not going the Samuel Haight-route - rather than Munchkining, the result should be thematically intriguing and suitable for play in some way.<br /> I hope to find some inspiration in your ideas, and hope that some of my write-ups will likewise cause someone's wheels to start turning.<br /> <br /> <br /> Something I thought might be fun: <b>Kindred/Begotten</b><br /> Rather than a human, a Vampire is plagued by recurring Nightmares, and when the Horror tries to Devour the willing Kindred, their very own Beast rears its head in greeting. However, the vampiric Soul is quite dissimilar from a human's - stronger in some ways, weaker in others. As a result, the Devouring is imperfect, and rather than a common Beast, the result is something different: an incarnation of vampiric fears inhabiting an undead body. A Nightmare of the Burning Sun, Eternal Hunger or Endless Servitude, rather than a Nightmare of Powerlessness, Darkness, Repulsion etc.<br /> In the wake of their Horror<br /> These <i>Scourges </i>Feed on Kindred rather than humans (although Low-integrity humans qualify as meals, too) and teach Lessons of Loss and Humanity, to forever remind their undead Kin that they are glorified parasites who have lost so much more than they gained.<br /> A Scourge can mechanically be treated like Vampire, except for the following points:<br /> - they have access to a Lair and Lair traits, but do not gain immunity to traits other than the ones they themselves inflict upon the world (a Scourge with Burning WILL burn like any other Kindred in a burning building, but is immune to the flames they call down in a dark room). In addition, the Blazing Sun Lair Trait is no longer available. They can only open Primordial Pathways to a Chamber they have claimed, or it's physical location.<br /> - furthermore, they have access to one Family's Atavisms (chosen at creation), but lose access to any and all in-Clan or Bloodline-restricted Disciplines.<br /> - their Blood tastes kind of bland - to other Kindred, they are clan-less. Due to that, they do not have a clan-specific Weakness. Instead, Heroes may place Anathema on them when they are Sated.<br /> - they do not have an Integrity stat, and fuel their abilities from both Vitae and their Horror's Satiety. Their Power Stat is Blood Potency. They need Vitae to function like a normal Kindred, but also to stabilize the bloody nightmare that is their Lair \u2013 they need to spent an additional Vitae per day as upkeep for the Lair. When Starving, the body needs another Vitae to function.<br /> - a Scourge may sate her Horror with Vitae \u2013 converting 7 Vitae into purest life essence allows raising the Satiety by 1, once per night. The Horror will not be satisfied with any further attempts.<br /> - Scourges do not enter Frenzy, unless they are Starving.<br /> - When Ravenous, a Scourge is, for all purposes, a mindless monster under the control of his Horror.<br /> - Scourges cannot learn Coils/Scales of the Dragon or Miracles, but instead can learn Obcasus Rites<br /> - Scourges can immediately refill both Vitae and Satiety by Amaranth, in addition to it's usual benefits.<br /> Thoughts? What else needs to be addressed/detailed?<br /> Other concepts that will be posted some time later:<br /> Begotten/Kindred - modified Ghoul template (<i>Fiends </i>as a name, I thought)<br /> Kindred/Mage - Pattern-devouring, reality-consuming eldritch willworkers (<i>Bloodmages</i>?)<br /> Begotten/Uratha - lliteral shapeshifting horrors (<i>Shoggoths</i>! =D)<br /> Uratha/Begotten - Werewolf-hunting <i>J\u00e4ger</i>, Nightmares of Silver Collars, of crumbling Walls, of Isolation and Stagnation.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T11:35:54-07:00","id":1198781,"title":"","content":"ammm the main thing that I'll change to the vampire/ begotten hybrid is that instead of it being a vampire Devoured by an Horror, I would have tied the Embrace and the Devouring into the same event- for example, a vampire who is haunted by nightmares Embrace a mortal- only for the mortal in question to be Devoured by something far older and dangerous. Or perhaps we could make it into a Revanant which is Uplifted by an Horror instead of a Kindred. So it is less about &quot;harnessing a new Template&quot; as much as &quot;gaining a modified/hybrid template&quot;.<br /> <br /> As for Kindred/Mage, I think that's what the Sons of Phobos and the Tremere are for (each from a different angle). There was also in the forums a version for a Demon/Mage hybrid, but it seems like I haven't bookmarked it.<br /> <br /> EDIT- so after a short search, I've found a number of draft for such hybrid templates:<br /> <br /> - The <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/996449-weird-experiment-changeling-meets-requiem-the-admonitoria\">Admonitoria </a>(the original which has started the all thing, Changeling/Vampire)<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1032485-mystery-fae-warlocks-of-arcadia-crossover-template-brainstorming\">Warlocks </a>(Changeling/Mage hybrid, by Satchel)<br /> -<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1183663-hybrid?p=1184640#post1184640\"> Kindy Ones</a> (Changeling/Beast, by Mad Maudlin)<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/999372-between-descent-and-awakening-the-ravani\">Ravani </a>(Demon/Mage, by Caladriu)<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1034495-soul-a-subjective-fuel-stat-for-the-tremere\">Tremere </a>(Vampire/Mage version, by Inodiv)<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1194311-contagion-chronicles-awakening-the-beast?p=1198219#post1198219\">Crones and Wyrms</a> (Beast/Mage, by Second Chances)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","user":"LostLight","date":". 03-23-2018, 03:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T12:27:07-07:00","id":1198794,"title":"","content":"An easy way to do Awakened Werewolf, or at least justify it, might be to have them become like a Pangaean, through the gathering of omphalos stones or devouring of Pangaean carcasses.<br /> <br /> I believe Guayota, or at least his plot hook, would be a way to do werewolf/mummy or even werewolf/sin-eater.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1169158-twelve-storm-lords-bowing?p=1169611#post1169611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Guayota has become a disembodied spirit, roving far and wide on strange and bizarre affairs. Now, however, it has returned its attention to the real world, and wishes to return to existence. It is manipulating the Tibicenas into performing something akin to the Rite of Return used by the Shaniatu of Irem, having pried that lore loose from the world on its travels. It plans to establish itself as a ghost-king, with the Tibicenas as cursed wolf-mummies grovelling before its throne.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-23-2018, 03:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T12:42:07-07:00","id":1198803,"title":"","content":"rewritting the Hollow as Mummy/Vampire seems like it may have some interesting potential, IMO.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T15:07:49-07:00","id":1198858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1198723-awakening-kindred-devoured-werewolves-and-other-hybrids?p=1198781#post1198781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1034495-soul-a-subjective-fuel-stat-for-the-tremere\">Tremere </a>(Vampire/Mage version, by Inodiv)</div> </div> </div> </div>A more fleshed out version can be found <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1SDefVkEBo8FVzgEx6RUwvsL3EUHZmk4syoa2LVMLjTo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> It's a forever WIP, but I've done a fair amount of playtesting and it works. Mr. Gone was also kind enough to make a sheet for it, which should be hosted on his site.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T17:34:38-07:00","id":1198909,"title":"","content":"The Kindly Ones probably need a revision in light of the Beast Player's Guide.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13641-mad_maudlin","name":"Mad_Maudlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T21:25:49-07:00","id":1199295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1198723-awakening-kindred-devoured-werewolves-and-other-hybrids?p=1198781#post1198781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT- so after a short search, I've found a number of draft for such hybrid templates:</div> </div> </div> </div>- The <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\">Genius</a> (Demon/Mage hybrid, by Milo v3)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-25T02:15:29-07:00","id":1199332,"title":"","content":"Awesome! <br /> Thanks everyone for the Contributions so far!<br /> I gave quite a lot of respect for the amount of work those long writeups take.<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar503_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"503\" data-vbnamecard=\"503\">LostLight</a> That is perfectly fair. I think there is a lot of room for different concepts: a revenant uplifted by a Devouring Could Result In Something Different From A Beast being embraced, or a Kindred being devoured, or even a mortal experiencing the Devouring during that Brief moment in between life and Death in the embrace. (Or stranger ways still - a Beast bathing in kindred vitae in a magical rite, a Kindred diablerizing a Horror, etc..)<br /> My approach was to try and take the idea that Begotten are fears made Manifest, and trying to apply that to Kindred -specific fears. Still needs work, needs more thought putninto it as it was a Spur of the moment thing, but I think it's a good concept, in and of itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-25T06:19:14-07:00","id":1199354,"title":"","content":"Other hybrid concepts (lacking material so far):<ul><li><b>Demon + Werewolf</b> - Demon calls in a Soul Pact <i>just</i> before or during a First Change; An Offspring/Fractal undergoes the First-Change and it super-charges their Demon blood as well; An Angel possesses someone undergoing the First Change and ends up Fallen, fused, and blended with the new Werewolf; Something funky happening with a Demon as the Totem of a Pack;</li> <li><b>Werewolf + Mage</b> - Soul-theft shenanigans involving a Werewolf; The &quot;lucky&quot; individual undergoes the First Change <i>while</i> in their Mystery Play; Weird interactions of a Spirit-based Legacy, acting as the Totem for a Pack, and a bad Totem's Wrath (Wolf Gift Facet).</li> <li><b>Demon + Vampire</b> - Cover Embraced while the Demon was Going Native or Play Possum; Ordo Dracul researcher gets too happy with grafting Demonic Form parts to themselves and &quot;reactivates&quot; them; Strix Synthesis fun;</li> <li><b>Promethean + Demon</b> - Guess whose parts were used for that Frankenstein or Unfleshed?; Demon accepts an offer from a powerful Quashmallim;</li> <li><b>Promethean + Mage</b> - Body used was of a Lich (of a resurrecting variety), and the returning spirit agrees to joint custody;</li> <li><b>Geist + Mage</b> - Geist fuses with a Ghost-Mage before or after the Bargain;</li> <li><b>Geist + Demon</b> - When the Geist came from an Echo;</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 03-25-2018, 09:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-25T08:29:50-07:00","id":1199384,"title":"","content":"Demon + Promethean makes me Wonder how to pull of a fallen Quashmallim. It would be closer to a new template, I guess, but still.<br /> <br /> <br /> If you wanna go crazy cross-over:<br /> A mage died, his body was turned into a promethean, but his ghost Hung on, turning into a Geist. Some time After the promethean achieved the New dawn, he died, and the original then soul now Geist makes the bargain. Rather than a normal sin-eater the result is.... something else. But it has the death arcana","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-25T09:09:40-07:00","id":1199391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1198723-awakening-kindred-devoured-werewolves-and-other-hybrids?p=1199354#post1199354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Geist + Mage</b> - Geist fuses with a Ghost-Mage before or after the Bargain;</div> </div> </div> </div>This is definitely something I'd like to write once Geist 2e comes out. A ghost-mage who somehow (possibly by drinking from a peculiar River) gains the Bargain Manifestation and changes the Geist-dependent part of the Bound template.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-25T09:32:54-07:00","id":1199396,"title":"","content":"So just to add my two fils on the topic, one thing that I've noticed is that if you try and mash two splats together, you create lots of complexity very quickly. When I try to create a mashup, what I do is mash a splat with a demisplat. So when I created the Crones and Wyrms, I combined a Beast with a Proximus. Part of that was due to Mage metaphysics, a Mage can't be devoured and a Beast can't awaken, but it is also because Proximi Blessings are much easier to substitute for Nightmares or Atavisms than full Arcana would be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-25T14:51:51-07:00","id":1199487,"title":"","content":"Another, less overt method of mixing would be giving a splat aspects of the other without actually porting in powers. Like vampires with weakness to iron and powers over illusions and binding-your-promises, but referring to none of actual Contracts and pledges from changelings. Easier said, I know, but just throwing ideas here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-25T15:10:50-07:00","id":1199497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1198723-awakening-kindred-devoured-werewolves-and-other-hybrids?p=1199396#post1199396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So just to add my two fils on the topic, one thing that I've noticed is that if you try and mash two splats together, you create lots of complexity very quickly. When I try to create a mashup, what I do is mash a splat with a demisplat. So when I created the Crones and Wyrms, I combined a Beast with a Proximus. Part of that was due to Mage metaphysics, a Mage can't be devoured and a Beast can't awaken, but it is also because Proximi Blessings are much easier to substitute for Nightmares or Atavisms than full Arcana would be.</div> </div> </div> </div>I may need to take a closer look at Mages, because Crones and (especially) Wyrms look badass.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-25T15:35:26-07:00","id":1199507,"title":"","content":"I would personally not include Mummies(Rite of Return wise anyway, got no problem with Lifeless failures to duplicate the Rite though) in this but beyond that, go hog wild. In particularly I feel like there is tons of room for God Machine hybrid horrors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-26T00:56:49-07:00","id":1199626,"title":"","content":"I could imagine a direct descendant of Kamduis or Isim-Ur turning out to be a Geist/Werewolf hybrid. They'd be called Cerberii, because they'd have &quot;three heads&quot;: one for the material, one for the Shadow, one for the Underworld. Probably known for their moral conundrums, since they'd have a three-axis Harmony scale. Possibly able to treat Underworld gates as Verges, and vice versa.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11431-adrasalieth","name":"Adrasalieth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-26T03:04:37-07:00","id":1199645,"title":"","content":"The sub-splat thing is a good pointer.<br /> Ghoul with minor Lair traits, Satiety rather than vitae (able to spent it on Disciplines) + Passing/Family resemblance and Nightmares could be a fun starting point.<br /> <br /> Wolf Blooded with a free Skin Deep Atavism, and the Skeleton Key, would be a nice alternative 'shapeshifter'.<br /> I will try to work these out some more!<br /> <br /> <br /> Re my kindred/mage: I wanted to less use the concept of stealing life to extended one's own, and more try to combine the themes of a Parasitic existance and reality-shifting Hubristic willworkers. That left, in my mind, the concept of Pattern-devouring parasites on reality, who can get their refill by weakening the foundation of reality (maybe According to their arcana, even) and inflicting a Tilt on the area, and Suffer from a similar fuel bleed as kindred, forcing them to repeatedly weaken the Fabric of reality. Similarly to prometheans, staying in one area very long would make it worse, causing Abyssal incursions, Gates to the hedge/underworld/Dream/Shadow/etc to open and similar shenanigans (tilts that make matter in the area lack substance, Forces to be wonky - giving Gas increases Temperature rather than speed-, propability off, thoughts diffuse, animals lethargic, etc).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","user":"Wormwood","date":".  Mobile Auto correct ' s a pain... 03-26-2018, 12:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-26T05:23:25-07:00","id":1199665,"title":"","content":"The endless possibilities make me giddy","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-26T07:18:29-07:00","id":1199708,"title":"","content":"A couple ideas I didn't really had the time to flesh out. <br /> <b>Changeling + Promethean</b>: A Fetch that receives an Elpis Vision and acquires the Divine Fire, effectively becoming a peculiar kind of Extempore. How will Disquiet affect the Mask? What will help the new creature's Pilgrimage: strive to imitate the person he thought he was, or become someone else entirely? <br /> <br /> <b>Mummy + Vampire</b>: The Deceived Utterance \u201cCall Down the Black Huriyah\u201d (Book of the Deceived, p.98) specifically refer to winged, shadowy entities that partially existed in Duat: a clear analogous for the Strix. I still have to figure how to work this around, though.<br /> <br /> <b>Mummy + Mage</b>: The Ehaiu (\u201ccriers\u201d) were professionals mourners in Ancient Egypt. That term could designate mages with the ability to localize Sebayt, and whose Shadow Name would also be a Keshina.<br /> <br /> <b>Mummy + Beast</b>: Ammut can easily be seen as another facet of the Dark Mother. So possibly, a Beast that can learn Bane Affinities instead of Nightmares, and who can birth Amkhata Horrorspawn.<br /> <br /> <b>Mummy + Changeling</b>: A Sadikh that became Fae-Touched (I don't know if it's still a thing, but anyway) after trying to follow his patron, taken into the Hedge by a True Fae. Now, he's able to Hedge-Spin low-level Relics together. His latest feat? Cobble together old pieces of pyropus along with other arcane reagents, and produce a perfect fac-simile of a Token of Reprieve. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11431-adrasalieth","name":"Adrasalieth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-26T07:25:46-07:00","id":1199711,"title":"","content":"An idea I had some time ago was a werewolf lodge that emulated heroes to hunt Beasts. I called it the Lodge of Herakles in my head.<br /> <br /> So basically, werewolf Heroes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-26T07:31:49-07:00","id":1199713,"title":"","content":"Mummy + Geist could be something nice to explore by tying it to the Twice Arisen process going bad- perhaps the ghost of the destined vessel proved itself stronger than it should have been, and forced the Mummy to Bargain for the right to dwell in its body. Perhaps it was found/has eaten/ was eaten by a Geist, which has allowed it to resurrect even though its cult has abandoned it. At any case, I can't seem to think that the Judges would be extremely happy about it :P<br /> <br /> Promethean + Mage feels like it should be more of Mage/Alchemist, as someone who has Awakened to the Divine Fire and was transformed by it. If one were to really want to preserve the Created part, perhaps something like that construct from Unbidden could be used as an inspiration- a Promethean like creature, powered by the Supernal instead of the Fire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-26T08:28:02-07:00","id":1199720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Adrasalieth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1198723-awakening-kindred-devoured-werewolves-and-other-hybrids?p=1199708#post1199708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A couple ideas I didn't really had the time to flesh out.<br /> <br /> <b>Mummy + Vampire</b>: The Deceived Utterance \u201cCall Down the Black Huriyah\u201d (Book of the Deceived, p.98) specifically refer to winged, shadowy entities that partially existed in Duat: a clear analogous for the Strix. I still have to figure how to work this around, though.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This sounds fascinating, and I'd like to subscribe to your newsletter. Actually I have an NPC in my current efforts who is a) very very old, b) presently encountered only in dreams or the spirit world (or, similar places), because his body was destroyed by the main campaign antagonist centuries before. Have used explicit strix imagery to impose a blend. Anyway, I know virtually nothing about Mummy in CofD, but am curious is something of a blend with vamps would resonate with what I've been noodling over.<br /> <br /> The Tremere document lays out some very interesting antagonists as well--especially for a Mage game. They retain the very flexible magic of the Arcana, and in that regard are a huge step up over, say, WoD Tremere. I wonder if a mix of Vamp+Proximi would come closer to the debased magical existence of the &quot;original&quot; WoD Tremere (mainly vamps, but with an affinity for rote spell-like effects and rituals), in which case in high irony such critters could hunt/agitate against the existence of &quot;soul-eaters&quot; (Salubri) per the document. <br /> <br /> Crossing the streams is fun.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","